  "direction": "Canonical IS_ORDERED_RIGHT_AFTER alias <; means Host follows Target; inverse alias IS_ORDERED_RIGHT_BEFORE alias ;> means Host precedes Target. Both write one model-order fact.",
  "admission": "Both named directions receive separate model-only 0..1 permissions for Atom.Header.** and Atom.Content.**; Relation prose requires same immediate bearer. No runtime Property-instance permission is introduced.",
  "syntax": "R2798 preserves standalone ; as expression separator and recognizes contiguous ;> and <; as whole ordering tokens.",
  "dependencies": [
    "Review exact selector scope, acyclic sibling adjacency and both explicit named outgoing permissions; preserve Current and Draft source alignment.",
    "Canonical Relation and inverse-alias binding require R2951 and existing alias() authority.",
    "Root owns Current source revisions, predecessor archives, ID allocation and subsequent coordinated migration; no parser implementation is implied."
  ],
  "limits": "No native Current/Draft, code, tests, Workflow, Workbench, Git or ID allocation."
